# {{BRAND_NAME}}

{{POSITIONING}}

Style: **{{STYLE_NAME}}** · Tagline: **{{TAGLINE}}** · Central metaphor: {{METAPHOR}}

Every choice in this package has to be justifiable by that metaphor. If a proposal cannot be, it is off-brand however good it looks.

## Working order

1. Read `prompts/BRAND-SYSTEM-PROMPT.md` first — it is self-contained and enough to produce on-brand work with no other context.
2. `README.md` is the full rulebook when you need the reasoning behind a rule.
3. Use `tokens/*.css` as-is. Never hard-code a hex that exists as a token, and never edit the token files by hand — they are generated from `brand.json`.
4. `brand.json` is the single source of truth. Changing a colour means changing it there and rebuilding: `python3 scripts/build_brand.py brand.json`.
5. `guidelines.html` is the printable specimen — open it to see the system rendered rather than described.
6. Logo assets are in `assets/`. Clear-space and minimum size are stated in `README.md`; if a placement needs a value that is not written down, ask rather than inventing one.

